<title>BELGIUM: EU takes 7,918 tonnes beef into intervention store.</title>
<headline>EU takes 7,918 tonnes beef into intervention store.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union's beef management committee accepted bids to sell 7,918 tonnes of beef into intervention stores at a maximum price of 266 Ecus a tonne, the European Commission said on Friday.</p>
<p>The total included 229 tonnes of beef from young store cattle at a maximum price of 355.99 Ecus a tonne, it said after an EU beef management committee meeting.</p>
</text>
